# device-layer-0025.
# The person's photo library, read: PhotoKit on macOS and iOS, the MediaStore provider on Android. A browser holds no
# photo library of the person's, so it answers `unavailable`.
#
#   find-photos(count)   the newest `count` photos, newest first, one a line: the platform's own identifier, a tab,
#                        when it was taken (else added), in UTC to the second, a tab, and its size as `<width>x<height>`
#                        in pixels. Or none (the library holds no photo)
#   copy-photo(id)       `photo <where>`: the photo as a JPEG file the app may read, at its full size, whatever the
#                        library keeps it as (HEIC, PNG). Or absent (no photo has that identifier)
#
# Each also answers not-determined (ask first: request-permission photos), denied, unavailable or failed. Access the
# person limited to some photos is a grant, and answers those. `count` is held to 1 through `most-photos`.
#
# A host with no such capability (the server, the memory host) answers `unavailable`. Every answer is text from the
# closed sets above, or the lines, so an app compares strings and no platform type ever reaches it.

load ./native/{platform}/photos
  find newest-photos
  find export-photo

# the most photos one call lists
host most-photos
  like number
  code 500

task find-photos
  take count, like number
  like text
  save held, read count
  fork test
    hook test
      call is-below
        read count
        code 1
    hook hold
      save held, code 1
  fork test
    hook test
      call is-above
        read count
        read most-photos
    hook hold
      save held, read most-photos
  send back
    call newest-photos
      read held

task copy-photo
  take id, like text
  like text
  send back
    call export-photo
      read id
